.TH ACER\-POWERSAVE 1 "September 2026" "1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
acer\-powersave \- hardware and power management for Acer Predator and Nitro laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acer\-powersave
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Applies the power settings that match the active profile of
.BR power\-profiles\-daemon (8),
keeping no state of its own on disk: the PPD profile is the single source of
truth. Under KDE, PowerDevil already maps AC and battery to a profile, so this
follows the mains cable and still honours a manual override.
.PP
It also corrects the CPU frequency cap that PPD applies in its power\-saver
profile. On this hardware that cap is counterproductive: measured on a
PH315\-53, the same task takes 3.25 times longer and burns 3.3 times more
energy, because the CPU cannot race to idle. See
.B unpin_cpu_freq
in the configuration file to turn the correction off.
.PP
It does not touch screen brightness.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Follows the active power\-profiles\-daemon profile and applies the privileged
settings. This is what
.B acer\-powersave.service
runs.
.TP
.B status
Shows power draw, profile, governor, EPP, frequency, turbo, ASPM, and the state
of the discrete GPU and the fans.
.TP
.BI measure " [seconds]"
Measures median idle power draw, discarding samples taken while the CPU was
busy so that comparing two configurations means something. Defaults to 30
seconds. Also accepts the older name
.BR medir .
.TP
.BI gpu " on\fR|\fPoff"
Powers the NVIDIA Optimus GPU up or down while the system is running, with no
reboot. Requires root.
.IP
With the GPU off there is no HDMI output on models where the port hangs off the
discrete card, which is the case on the PH315\-53. Run
.B gpu on
before plugging a monitor in.
.TP
.B fan
Applies a fan curve with hysteresis, read from
.IR /etc/acer\-powersave/profiles.conf .
Needs the linuwu_sense module. Requires root.
.TP
.BI charge-limit " PERCENT"
Stops charging at the given percentage, from 80 to 100, and records it in the
configuration file so that it survives a reboot. Requires root. Also accepts
the older name
.BR tope\-carga .
.IP
Writing the sysfs attribute directly does the same thing and needs no root:
the package hands it to the
.B linuwu_sense
group. The running daemon notices the change and records it, so the limit
survives a reboot either way.
.IP
The firmware only knows two states: battery health mode on, which cuts the
charge around 80%, and off, which charges to the top. Anything in between is
the driver watching the capacity. With health mode on the battery settles at
78-79%, never at a clean 80, which is why 80 is the lowest limit accepted.
.TP
.BI save-curve " MIN_TEMP CURVE"
Writes a fan curve to the configuration file. Invoked by the graphical
interface through polkit; rarely useful by hand. Also accepts the older name
.BR guardar\-curva .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/acer-powersave/profiles.conf
Settings applied for each profile, including the charge limit. Keys are
documented in the file itself.
.TP
.I /sys/class/power_supply/BAT1/charge_control_end_threshold
The charge limit itself, published by the linuwu_sense module under the name
the kernel already defines for it. Writing to it applies the limit but does
not record it.
.TP
.I /etc/default/grub.d/50-acer-powersave.cfg
Recommended kernel command line parameters.
.SH NOTES
To find out whether the discrete GPU is powered down, read sysfs.
.BR lspci (8)
and
.BR nvidia\-smi (1)
wake the PCIe bridge up and give you a false reading:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cat /sys/bus/pci/devices/0000:00:01.0/power_state
.RE
.fi
.PP
By default the card is kept out of the PCI bus from boot, which saves about
500 mW. See
.BR acer-powersave (1)
README.Debian for how to change that.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acer\-powersave\-session (1),
.BR blink (1),
.BR powerprofilesctl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Antonio Orizondo Leyva
